WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:01.694
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.694 --> 00:00:02.670
- Before we say goodbye,

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:05.160
I have a fun story from the
internet that I hope you enjoy.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.506
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:09.266
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.266 --> 00:00:12.300
We all know age is a
mentality, not just a number.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.080
So when do we officially
become old is the question.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.060
A middle school teacher
in Southern California

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.180
decided to ask his students
this question in a TikTok.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.550
You have to see these responses,

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:27.035
this one says, when you use Candy Crush

00:00:27.035 --> 00:00:27.900
(audience laughing)

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.027
which I don't know what that
is, so I guess I'm not old.

00:00:30.027 --> 00:00:32.250
Here's another,

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.990
when you have fun at Home Depot,

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:37.211
you know what?
(audience laughing)

00:00:37.211 --> 00:00:38.883
It's a great store.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.420
I love Home Depot and Lowe's, whatever.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.070
One student wrote,

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.410
you're old when people have to explain

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.050
social media references to you,

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:52.020
they even illustrated it
with a cartoon which was

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.910
just even more aggressive.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:55.749
And my personal favorite,

00:00:55.749 --> 00:00:57.810
when you start enjoying raisins.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:02.550
So, I liked raisins since
as a child, whatever.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.620
Shane is the 7th grade teacher

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.090
who collected these responses.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.260
We have him on the line right now

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.910
watching on Palm Springs KESQ-TV.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:11.933
What's up Shane?

00:01:13.274 --> 00:01:14.610
- Hi Kelly, how are you?

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.428
- Well, I love Home Depot, Shane.

00:01:16.428 --> 00:01:17.490
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.950
Which one of these got you the most?

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.140
- So for me, I really, in for me

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.460
it was a Candy Crush question

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.830
simply because I play Candy Crush.

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:28.140
And so here I am at like level 300

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.710
thinking that I am killing the
game only to then learn that

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:35.700
that unfortunately makes me
old in the eyes of my students.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.400
But for me, this really
goes back to the idea of why

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.200
I love teaching middle school.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.040
It really is a case of
expect the unexpected.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.100
And I think middle schoolers
are really just at that age

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.140
where they're starting
to come into their own,

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:52.170
starting to begin that
journey of self-discovery.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.690
And I think that that's a
large reason why so many people

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:57.990
have come to love the
content that we have produced

00:01:57.990 --> 00:01:59.370
because it's super relatable,

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.720
people think that it's funny

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.420
and people enjoy the
perspective of middle schoolers.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.240
- It is really funny,
except Home Depots. Awesome.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.750
Has your TikTok made you
popular now with your students?

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:12.120
- So my students ask
if I am a celebrity now

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.280
because of all the viral
videos that we have produced.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.880
And of course I would love
to be paid like a celebrity

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.700
but for me it's all just a matter of fun.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.000
I'm always trying to
leverage what is, you know,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.250
current and contemporary
in the outside world

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.960
and bring it into the classroom.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:31.530
I think now more than ever,
especially post pandemic,

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:32.700
one of the biggest issues

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.710
that we as educators are struggling with

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:37.920
is simply trying to engage students again.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.440
I think, you know, trying to build that,

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.850
the idea of building community,

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:44.520
trying to get kids engaged
and creating an environment

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:47.760
where kids want to
participate and just have fun.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.500
So while I think that,

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.360
yes, these videos definitely provide me

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:55.260
some clout in the classroom,
that definitely is really cool.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.400
And at the end of the day

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.673
I'm a guest on the Kelly
Clarkson Talk Show.

00:02:58.673 --> 00:02:59.978
(Kelly laughing)
(audience cheering)

00:02:59.978 --> 00:03:03.510
- Oh my god, Shane, thank you
so much for being an educator.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.690
And junior high can be a tough,
a tough time for teachers.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:09.390
And my mom, she did
junior high for a minute,

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.670
substitute teaching before she
stuck to elementary school.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:14.370
And that could be a hard,
a hard time for teachers.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:16.970
So thank you so much, it's
a cool thing that you do.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.060
I'm liking your posts
right now, right man.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:22.553
Well that's not all though,

00:03:22.553 --> 00:03:24.930
our season long partner
pilot pin makers of FriXion,

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.210
the go-to race ball pen
of the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:29.280
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.440
and engaging students just like you.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.940
So they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.060
How's that sound?
(audience cheering)

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.720
- Oh my gosh, thank you so much.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.274
Absolutely. Thank you.

00:03:38.274 --> 00:03:39.107
- Thank you Shane.

00:03:39.107 --> 00:03:40.560
And thank you to all our guests today,

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.290
Benjamin Grant, Nikki
Glaser, Jake Viramontez,

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.450
Dustin Lee and Emily Coffman.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.350
Y'all have a great day and if
it's not, try and change it.

